1
00:00:00,342 --> 00:00:03,317
Last video ended with these thousand simulated bags

2
00:00:03,337 --> 00:00:03,719
of chips.

3
00:00:04,322 --> 00:00:06,249
The machine aims for one hundred and seventy-five

4
00:00:06,291 --> 00:00:06,671
grams.

5
00:00:07,174 --> 00:00:09,338
Most bags land close to that, a few

6
00:00:09,399 --> 00:00:10,321
land further away,

7
00:00:10,823 --> 00:00:12,826
and the two sides look like mirror images.

8
00:00:13,490 --> 00:00:14,677
Watch a few more bags fill.

9
00:00:15,301 --> 00:00:17,489
Each one gets about ninety chips, and each

10
00:00:17,570 --> 00:00:19,617
chip is a little heavier or lighter than

11
00:00:19,658 --> 00:00:20,099
the last.

12
00:00:20,984 --> 00:00:24,171
Heights, measurement errors and many other natural measurements

13
00:00:24,352 --> 00:00:25,955
often make a similar bell shape.

14
00:00:26,557 --> 00:00:28,074
So why does it keep turning up?

15
00:00:28,540 --> 00:00:29,707
When can we use it as a model?

16
00:00:30,130 --> 00:00:31,477
And what does its shape tell us?

17
00:00:32,269 --> 00:00:33,012
Here's one reason.

18
00:00:33,717 --> 00:00:36,086
A bag's mass isn't set by one thing.

19
00:00:36,628 --> 00:00:38,551
Lots of small effects push it a little

20
00:00:38,632 --> 00:00:41,055
up or a little down, like one more

21
00:00:41,096 --> 00:00:43,499
chip, a bigger chip, or a few crumbs.

22
00:00:44,363 --> 00:00:46,870
Watch dots fall through twelve rows of pegs.

23
00:00:47,694 --> 00:00:49,920
Each peg nudges a dot left or right,

24
00:00:50,241 --> 00:00:50,983
with equal chance.

25
00:00:51,825 --> 00:00:53,868
To land at the far left, a dot

26
00:00:53,909 --> 00:00:56,272
has to go left all twelve times, and

27
00:00:56,313 --> 00:00:57,615
only one path does that.

28
00:00:58,498 --> 00:01:00,462
To land one bin in from the edge,

29
00:01:00,884 --> 00:01:02,607
it needs just one right nudge,

30
00:01:03,109 --> 00:01:04,612
and that nudge can come at any of

31
00:01:04,653 --> 00:01:07,038
the twelve rows, so twelve paths do.

32
00:01:07,942 --> 00:01:10,128
To land in the middle, it needs six

33
00:01:10,169 --> 00:01:11,552
of each, in any order,

34
00:01:12,175 --> 00:01:14,000
and nine hundred and twenty-four paths do that.

35
00:01:14,943 --> 00:01:16,826
So the dots pile up in the middle

36
00:01:17,208 --> 00:01:18,629
and thin out towards the edges,

37
00:01:19,151 --> 00:01:20,252
the same on both sides.

38
00:01:21,135 --> 00:01:24,400
When many small, independent effects add up, the

39
00:01:24,442 --> 00:01:26,585
total often has a shape close to a

40
00:01:26,626 --> 00:01:26,845
bell.

41
00:01:27,595 --> 00:01:29,824
The smooth bell that fits this shape is

42
00:01:29,886 --> 00:01:31,492
called the normal distribution.

43
00:01:32,136 --> 00:01:35,077
It's a continuous probability distribution, and it's used

44
00:01:35,098 --> 00:01:38,319
to model many naturally occurring things, like adult

45
00:01:38,360 --> 00:01:39,739
heights in one population,

46
00:01:40,261 --> 00:01:42,441
measurement errors, and products from a machine.

47
00:01:43,424 --> 00:01:45,647
A bag can have any mass, not just

48
00:01:45,828 --> 00:01:48,031
a whole number of grams, so the model

49
00:01:48,152 --> 00:01:49,935
is a smooth curve, not bars.

50
00:01:50,798 --> 00:01:53,063
Just as in the histogram, the area over

51
00:01:53,104 --> 00:01:54,506
an interval is the probability.

52
00:01:55,210 --> 00:01:56,396
The fit is never perfect.

53
00:01:57,020 --> 00:01:59,044
It's a model, worth trying when the data

54
00:01:59,085 --> 00:02:01,509
bunch symmetrically around one peak, and then the

55
00:02:01,571 --> 00:02:02,772
tails have to match too.

56
00:02:03,329 --> 00:02:04,555
So what does the shape mean?

57
00:02:05,279 --> 00:02:08,068
The curve is symmetric about its mean, mu.

58
00:02:08,854 --> 00:02:10,545
Fold it at mu and the two halves

59
00:02:10,606 --> 00:02:10,847
match.

60
00:02:11,532 --> 00:02:13,541
So half the area is on each side,

61
00:02:13,924 --> 00:02:15,873
which makes mu the median too.

62
00:02:16,656 --> 00:02:19,022
The curve is highest at mu, so mu

63
00:02:19,103 --> 00:02:20,065
is also the mode.

64
00:02:20,749 --> 00:02:23,366
Mean, median and mode are the same value.

65
00:02:23,989 --> 00:02:25,632
Most of the area sits close to the

66
00:02:25,653 --> 00:02:27,897
mean, and the curve gets lower and lower

67
00:02:28,019 --> 00:02:28,519
further out.

68
00:02:28,961 --> 00:02:30,966
That's why most bags land within a few

69
00:02:31,027 --> 00:02:32,410
grams of one seventy-five.

70
00:02:33,254 --> 00:02:35,284
Its tails get closer and closer to the

71
00:02:35,366 --> 00:02:36,913
axis, but never touch it.

72
00:02:37,557 --> 00:02:40,103
So the curve goes on forever, in both

73
00:02:40,144 --> 00:02:40,585
directions.

74
00:02:41,241 --> 00:02:43,792
We write X is normal, with mean mu

75
00:02:44,033 --> 00:02:46,022
and variance sigma squared, like this.

76
00:02:46,728 --> 00:02:47,901
The first number is the mean.

77
00:02:48,264 --> 00:02:49,629
The second is the variance,

78
00:02:50,151 --> 00:02:51,536
not the standard deviation.

79
00:02:52,218 --> 00:02:55,004
The bags are N of one seventy-five, sixteen,

80
00:02:55,225 --> 00:02:56,989
so sigma is the square root of sixteen,

81
00:02:57,029 --> 00:02:57,931
which is four grams.

82
00:02:58,675 --> 00:03:01,428
Change mu, and the whole bell slides along

83
00:03:01,469 --> 00:03:01,910
the axis.

84
00:03:02,534 --> 00:03:04,778
Make sigma bigger, and the bell spreads out

85
00:03:04,900 --> 00:03:07,284
and gets lower, because the total area has

86
00:03:07,325 --> 00:03:08,006
to stay one.

87
00:03:08,648 --> 00:03:09,791
Make it one and a half times as

88
00:03:09,872 --> 00:03:12,037
wide, and its peak drops to two thirds

89
00:03:12,059 --> 00:03:12,459
of the height.

90
00:03:13,283 --> 00:03:15,237
So when is a normal model useful?

91
00:03:16,042 --> 00:03:18,507
Look for continuous data that bunch around one

92
00:03:18,567 --> 00:03:21,053
peak and thin out evenly in both directions.

93
00:03:21,795 --> 00:03:23,800
Then lay the bell over the data and

94
00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:25,285
check that the tails match too.

95
00:03:26,067 --> 00:03:27,795
These are clues, not a proof.

96
00:03:28,619 --> 00:03:30,987
Many small, independent effects adding up is a

97
00:03:31,007 --> 00:03:31,429
good sign.

98
00:03:32,213 --> 00:03:33,758
Household water use isn't like that.

99
00:03:34,542 --> 00:03:36,246
Most homes use a moderate amount, but a

100
00:03:36,287 --> 00:03:38,392
few use a lot, so the tail stretches

101
00:03:38,473 --> 00:03:39,074
far to the right.

102
00:03:39,896 --> 00:03:41,681
The bus wait from two videos ago is

103
00:03:41,822 --> 00:03:42,825
flat, not a bell.

104
00:03:43,589 --> 00:03:46,080
And a component's lifetime piles up near zero,

105
00:03:46,463 --> 00:03:47,165
then trails off.

106
00:03:47,888 --> 00:03:49,493
For those, a normal model would put the

107
00:03:49,534 --> 00:03:50,998
probability in the wrong places.

108
00:03:51,748 --> 00:03:54,497
In a normal model, probability is still area.

109
00:03:55,120 --> 00:03:57,024
A bag is underweight if it holds less

110
00:03:57,065 --> 00:03:58,368
than one hundred and seventy grams.

111
00:03:58,991 --> 00:04:00,778
That's the area to the left of one

112
00:04:00,819 --> 00:04:02,747
seventy, and it runs all the way out

113
00:04:02,848 --> 00:04:03,851
to minus infinity.

114
00:04:04,535 --> 00:04:07,644
A single value has zero probability, so less

115
00:04:07,665 --> 00:04:09,912
than one seventy and at most one seventy

116
00:04:10,013 --> 00:04:10,955
give the same area.

117
00:04:11,679 --> 00:04:13,868
The model even gives a tiny area to

118
00:04:13,909 --> 00:04:16,218
impossible bags, like negative masses.

119
00:04:16,781 --> 00:04:18,385
For these bags, that area is so small

120
00:04:18,426 --> 00:04:20,250
it doesn't matter, so the model is still

121
00:04:20,352 --> 00:04:20,611
useful.

122
00:04:21,314 --> 00:04:22,998
A bag over one hundred and eighty grams

123
00:04:23,320 --> 00:04:25,003
is the area to the right, out to

124
00:04:25,064 --> 00:04:25,725
plus infinity.

125
00:04:26,368 --> 00:04:28,713
One eighty is five grams above the mean,

126
00:04:29,295 --> 00:04:31,119
and one seventy is five below.

127
00:04:31,621 --> 00:04:34,488
So by symmetry, these two tails have the

128
00:04:34,530 --> 00:04:35,190
same area.

129
00:04:35,834 --> 00:04:37,668
And the bags between them are what's left

130
00:04:37,750 --> 00:04:37,910
over.

131
00:04:38,516 --> 00:04:40,382
That's one, minus both tails.

132
00:04:41,266 --> 00:04:42,843
The mean splits the curve too.

133
00:04:43,489 --> 00:04:44,870
Each half is exactly a

134
00:04:45,412 --> 00:04:45,671
half,

135
00:04:46,173 --> 00:04:48,096
so the bags from one seventy up to

136
00:04:48,177 --> 00:04:51,202
one seventy-five are a half, minus that left

137
00:04:51,243 --> 00:04:51,522
tail.

138
00:04:52,145 --> 00:04:54,073
You can find all three regions from one

139
00:04:54,115 --> 00:04:55,943
tail, using nothing but the shape of the

140
00:04:55,984 --> 00:04:56,244
curve.

141
00:04:56,976 --> 00:04:58,403
Here's a way to remember the shape.

142
00:04:59,169 --> 00:04:59,530
Mirror,

143
00:05:00,053 --> 00:05:01,138
middle, forever.

144
00:05:01,982 --> 00:05:04,486
The halves mirror each other, the mean, median

145
00:05:04,607 --> 00:05:06,049
and mode share one middle,

146
00:05:06,590 --> 00:05:08,272
and the tails go on forever.

147
00:05:10,900 --> 00:05:11,370
Your turn.

148
00:05:11,838 --> 00:05:13,163
State these four values.

149
00:05:13,727 --> 00:05:14,551
Pause here to answer.

150
00:05:25,308 --> 00:05:27,855
The first number is the mean, so mu

151
00:05:27,996 --> 00:05:28,717
is sixty-four.

152
00:05:29,280 --> 00:05:31,601
The curve is symmetric with one peak, so

153
00:05:31,642 --> 00:05:33,923
the median and the mode are sixty-four too.

154
00:05:34,705 --> 00:05:37,355
The second number, thirty-six, is the variance.

155
00:05:37,899 --> 00:05:39,889
So sigma is the square root of thirty-six,

156
00:05:40,171 --> 00:05:41,357
which is six millimetres.

157
00:05:42,343 --> 00:05:44,533
A standard deviation of thirty-six is wrong.

158
00:05:45,037 --> 00:05:46,583
Thirty-six is sigma squared.

159
00:05:48,570 --> 00:05:49,000
Last one.

160
00:05:49,628 --> 00:05:50,818
Use the shape of the curve.

161
00:05:51,505 --> 00:05:52,436
Pause here to answer.

162
00:06:03,081 --> 00:06:05,712
Two fifty-eight is eight grams above the mean,

163
00:06:06,134 --> 00:06:08,282
and two forty-two is eight grams below.

164
00:06:09,125 --> 00:06:11,250
The curve is symmetric, so the right tail

165
00:06:11,310 --> 00:06:13,876
has the same area: zero point zero five

166
00:06:13,916 --> 00:06:14,357
four eight.

167
00:06:15,219 --> 00:06:17,825
The middle is one minus two lots of

168
00:06:17,865 --> 00:06:20,230
zero point zero five four eight, which is

169
00:06:20,411 --> 00:06:22,275
zero point eight nine zero four.

170
00:06:23,360 --> 00:06:25,573
One minus zero point zero five four eight

171
00:06:25,955 --> 00:06:26,377
is wrong.

172
00:06:26,861 --> 00:06:28,416
That removes only the left tail.

173
00:06:30,121 --> 00:06:33,447
So check the peak, symmetry and tails against

174
00:06:33,507 --> 00:06:34,168
the normal model,

175
00:06:34,790 --> 00:06:36,553
and a normal shape tells us the mean,

176
00:06:36,833 --> 00:06:38,837
median and mode are the same.

177
00:06:40,248 --> 00:06:41,359
Next, a new question.

178
00:06:42,024 --> 00:06:44,701
Mark one sigma either side of the mean.

179
00:06:45,406 --> 00:06:47,520
How much of the area lies between those

180
00:06:47,601 --> 00:06:47,903
marks?

181
00:06:48,528 --> 00:06:50,256
And what about two sigma, or three?

182
00:06:53,455 --> 00:06:54,338
Here are the key notes.

183
00:06:54,861 --> 00:06:56,629
Pause the video if you need more time

184
00:06:56,650 --> 00:06:57,131
to copy them.
